1
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:06,253
JESUS: A new commandment I give you.

2
00:00:06,603 --> 00:00:08,465
JESUS: My command is this:

3
00:00:08,665 --> 00:00:11,894
JESUS: Love each other... as I have loved you.

4
00:00:12,844 --> 00:00:16,173
He said this on the night He was betrayed...

5
00:00:16,273 --> 00:00:21,125
only moments after handing bread to the man who would betray Him.

6
00:00:25,875 --> 00:00:31,042
Behind this door, an old man waits to die... for the name of Jesus.

7
00:00:31,392 --> 00:00:36,157
And the man standing outside it... has hated him for most of his life.

8
00:00:38,206 --> 00:00:40,108
ASHER: Bread. I'm bringing him bread.

9
00:00:40,658 --> 00:00:42,444
ASHER: I don't even want to be here.

10
00:00:42,794 --> 00:00:45,266
ASHER: Why am I even here? This is foolish.

11
00:00:47,416 --> 00:00:51,854
Months earlier, in a house where followers of Jesus gathered...

12
00:00:51,904 --> 00:00:55,569
a letter from the apostle Paul was read aloud.

13
00:00:55,819 --> 00:01:00,559
PHOEBE: Paul, a servant of Christ Jesus... to all in Rome who are loved by God.

14
00:01:01,609 --> 00:01:04,193
PHOEBE: Do not repay anyone evil for evil.

15
00:01:04,443 --> 00:01:08,980
PHOEBE: If it is possible, as far as it depends on you... live at peace with everyone.

16
00:01:09,230 --> 00:01:14,228
PHOEBE: If your enemy is hungry, feed him. If he is thirsty, give him something to drink.

17
00:01:14,378 --> 00:01:17,620
PHOEBE: In doing this, you will heap burning coals on his head.

18
00:01:20,170 --> 00:01:21,470
ASHER: His own words.

19
00:01:22,120 --> 00:01:23,806
ASHER: Let's see if he believes them.

20
00:01:26,756 --> 00:01:28,651
GUARD: Food for the old man?

21
00:01:28,901 --> 00:01:32,056
GUARD: You're the first one in a week. Make it quick.

22
00:01:34,506 --> 00:01:36,974
PAUL: Luke! Is that you, my brother?

23
00:01:37,324 --> 00:01:40,035
PAUL: Come in, come in! Thank you for coming.

24
00:01:40,185 --> 00:01:43,399
PAUL: The Lord provides... He always provides.

25
00:01:43,649 --> 00:01:46,363
PAUL: And you've brought bread. God bless you.

26
00:01:46,613 --> 00:01:50,378
PAUL: So many are afraid to come now. I don't blame them.

27
00:01:50,528 --> 00:01:51,958
PAUL: But you came.

28
00:01:53,208 --> 00:01:54,334
ASHER: I'm not Luke.

29
00:01:54,784 --> 00:01:59,284
ASHER: But... thank you. For thinking I could be someone so dear to you.

30
00:01:59,934 --> 00:02:02,139
PAUL: Then who are you, my friend?

31
00:02:02,689 --> 00:02:06,884
ASHER: Someone you met once... in Jerusalem. A long time ago.

32
00:02:07,134 --> 00:02:10,379
ASHER: The street of the potters. A house with a blue door.

33
00:02:10,729 --> 00:02:13,675
ASHER: You came at night... with the temple guard.

34
00:02:14,325 --> 00:02:17,036
ASHER: You dragged a man named Yosef into the street.

35
00:02:17,186 --> 00:02:18,602
ASHER: In front of his wife.

36
00:02:18,652 --> 00:02:20,067
ASHER: In front of his son.

37
00:02:20,817 --> 00:02:22,341
PAUL: Yosef...

38
00:02:23,191 --> 00:02:27,723
ASHER: I was eight years old. I watched it all... through a crack in the door.

39
00:02:28,373 --> 00:02:30,025
ASHER: He never came home.

40
00:02:32,975 --> 00:02:34,584
PAUL: He looked at me.

41
00:02:35,134 --> 00:02:38,482
PAUL: When we bound his hands... he looked straight at me.

42
00:02:38,732 --> 00:02:41,673
PAUL: Not with hatred. I knew hatred.

43
00:02:42,023 --> 00:02:46,213
PAUL: He looked at me as if... as if he was sorry for me.

44
00:02:50,063 --> 00:02:51,682
YOUNG ASHER: Father! Don't go!

45
00:02:53,232 --> 00:02:56,769
YOSEF: Asher, my love... don't be afraid for me.

46
00:02:57,019 --> 00:03:00,917
YOSEF: I am in the hands of God. He will keep me...

47
00:03:00,967 --> 00:03:04,384
YOSEF: and He will keep you, forever and ever.

48
00:03:04,934 --> 00:03:05,824
PAUL: Take him!

49
00:03:07,374 --> 00:03:10,764
YOSEF: May God open your eyes, my son.

50
00:03:13,514 --> 00:03:14,374
ASHER: Don't.

51
00:03:14,624 --> 00:03:16,347
ASHER: You don't get to remember him.

52
00:03:16,797 --> 00:03:19,461
PAUL: I remember him because I must.

53
00:03:19,711 --> 00:03:24,276
PAUL: Every soul I wounded is a soul the Son came to save...

54
00:03:24,326 --> 00:03:27,583
PAUL: your father... and you... and even me.

55
00:03:27,933 --> 00:03:32,214
PAUL: I will spend every breath I have left proclaiming His mercy...

56
00:03:32,264 --> 00:03:36,736
PAUL: until it reaches all of them. Even the ones I lost.

57
00:03:38,486 --> 00:03:40,488
ASHER: They read your letter to us in Rome.

58
00:03:40,738 --> 00:03:43,394
ASHER: “If your enemy is hungry, feed him.”

59
00:03:43,744 --> 00:03:45,282
ASHER: So. I'm feeding you.

60
00:03:47,432 --> 00:03:50,562
PAUL: Then you have done what I only wrote about.

61
00:03:50,912 --> 00:03:53,042
ASHER: Spare me. Don't make me a saint.

62
00:03:53,292 --> 00:03:56,524
ASHER: They call you a saint. Do they even know what you were?

63
00:03:56,974 --> 00:03:58,077
PAUL: They know.

64
00:03:58,227 --> 00:04:02,015
PAUL: I put it in my letters, so that no one forgets.

65
00:04:02,365 --> 00:04:07,714
PAUL: I was a blasphemer... and a persecutor... and a violent man.

66
00:04:08,263 --> 00:04:10,865
PAUL: I thought I was defending God.

67
00:04:11,215 --> 00:04:12,986
PAUL: I was hunting Him.

68
00:04:13,736 --> 00:04:18,063
PAUL: I carried Yosef's face with me, all the way to Damascus.

69
00:04:18,313 --> 00:04:21,108
PAUL: I had letters to arrest more of them.

70
00:04:25,058 --> 00:04:28,635
JESUS: Paul... Paul. Why do you persecute me?

71
00:04:29,084 --> 00:04:30,701
PAUL: Who are you, Lord?

72
00:04:31,251 --> 00:04:36,100
JESUS: I am Jesus. I came to save those who are not yet saved.

73
00:04:37,050 --> 00:04:39,401
JESUS: You are precious to me, Paul.

74
00:04:39,551 --> 00:04:45,627
JESUS: Open your heart to me... and carry the Holy Spirit, with me and my Father.

75
00:04:46,177 --> 00:04:48,169
PAUL: I knew what I deserved.

76
00:04:48,519 --> 00:04:52,060
PAUL: But He looked at me... the same way Yosef had.

77
00:04:52,510 --> 00:04:57,493
PAUL: I was shown mercy, because I acted in ignorance and unbelief.

78
00:04:57,644 --> 00:05:01,629
PAUL: The grace of our Lord was poured out on me abundantly...

79
00:05:01,649 --> 00:05:06,030
PAUL: along with the faith and love that are in Christ Jesus.

80
00:05:06,380 --> 00:05:10,670
PAUL: I thank Christ Jesus our Lord, who has given me strength...

81
00:05:10,720 --> 00:05:15,239
PAUL: that He considered me trustworthy, appointing me to His service.

82
00:05:15,589 --> 00:05:19,333
PAUL: He chose me... the very one who hunted Him.

83
00:05:20,083 --> 00:05:21,258
ASHER: So that's it?

84
00:05:21,508 --> 00:05:24,183
ASHER: You saw a light... and it all washed away?

85
00:05:24,533 --> 00:05:28,058
ASHER: And my father was just... the price of your conversion?

86
00:05:28,708 --> 00:05:29,724
PAUL: No.

87
00:05:30,074 --> 00:05:33,404
PAUL: Nothing washes him away. Not for me.

88
00:05:33,754 --> 00:05:38,327
PAUL: I see his face every time I write the word “mercy.”

89
00:05:39,577 --> 00:05:44,186
PAUL: Here is a trustworthy saying that deserves full acceptance:

90
00:05:44,336 --> 00:05:48,224
PAUL: Christ Jesus came into the world to save sinners...

91
00:05:48,474 --> 00:05:50,951
PAUL: of whom I am the worst.

92
00:05:51,601 --> 00:05:54,941
PAUL: But for that very reason, I was shown mercy...

93
00:05:54,991 --> 00:05:58,512
PAUL: by Him, my Lord... the One who saved me...

94
00:05:58,662 --> 00:06:04,912
PAUL: so that in me, the worst of sinners, Christ Jesus might display His immense patience...

95
00:06:04,962 --> 00:06:10,548
PAUL: as an example for those who would believe in Him... and receive eternal life.

96
00:06:11,298 --> 00:06:12,938
ASHER: I came here to hate you.

97
00:06:13,488 --> 00:06:15,513
ASHER: I rehearsed it. For years.

98
00:06:15,863 --> 00:06:18,139
ASHER: You say all these beautiful things...

99
00:06:18,289 --> 00:06:21,109
ASHER: but I still hate you. I hope you know that.

100
00:06:21,759 --> 00:06:22,868
PAUL: I know.

101
00:06:23,217 --> 00:06:25,468
PAUL: And I will not hate you back.

102
00:06:25,818 --> 00:06:31,032
PAUL: Hate me, if you must. I will still pray for you, every day I have left...

103
00:06:31,082 --> 00:06:33,828
PAUL: and I will still call you my brother.

104
00:06:34,378 --> 00:06:35,816
ASHER: I am not your brother.

105
00:06:36,466 --> 00:06:38,315
PAUL: Not yet, perhaps.

106
00:06:38,565 --> 00:06:42,328
PAUL: But the Lord is patient. He was patient with me.

107
00:06:43,078 --> 00:06:44,236
ASHER: And still...

108
00:06:44,586 --> 00:06:45,972
ASHER: I brought the bread.

109
00:06:46,722 --> 00:06:52,300
JESUS: A new commandment I give you: love one another, as I have loved you.

110
00:06:59,250 --> 00:07:01,226
ASHER: I don't forgive you. Not yet.

111
00:07:01,776 --> 00:07:04,479
ASHER: But my father would have shared his bread with you...

112
00:07:04,629 --> 00:07:05,855
ASHER: so I will.

113
00:07:08,905 --> 00:07:10,714
PAUL: Burning coals...

114
00:07:11,264 --> 00:07:13,250
PAUL: I wrote those words...

115
00:07:13,400 --> 00:07:18,992
PAUL: I never knew how much the love of Christ would burn me... but for the better.

116
00:07:19,742 --> 00:07:22,446
Do not be overcome by evil...

117
00:07:22,696 --> 00:07:25,369
but overcome evil with good.

118
00:07:27,319 --> 00:07:28,576
GUARD: Time's up.

119
00:07:28,926 --> 00:07:32,881
GUARD: And you, old man... it's tomorrow. At first light.

120
00:07:33,831 --> 00:07:34,910
ASHER: Tomorrow?

121
00:07:35,360 --> 00:07:37,088
PAUL: Thank you, soldier.

122
00:07:37,338 --> 00:07:38,983
GUARD: Say your goodbyes.

123
00:07:39,933 --> 00:07:41,236
ASHER: Aren't you afraid?

124
00:07:42,186 --> 00:07:43,418
PAUL: Afraid?

125
00:07:43,769 --> 00:07:47,063
PAUL: Who shall separate us from the love of Christ?

126
00:07:47,313 --> 00:07:50,813
PAUL: Shall trouble, or hardship, or persecution...

127
00:07:50,833 --> 00:07:54,667
PAUL: or famine, or nakedness, or danger, or sword?

128
00:07:54,917 --> 00:07:59,292
PAUL: As it is written: “For your sake we face death all day long;

129
00:07:59,312 --> 00:08:02,578
PAUL: we are considered as sheep to be slaughtered.”

130
00:08:02,928 --> 00:08:06,674
PAUL: No! In all these things we are more than conquerors...

131
00:08:06,694 --> 00:08:09,074
PAUL: through Him who loved us.

132
00:08:09,424 --> 00:08:12,863
PAUL: For I am convinced that neither death nor life,

133
00:08:12,883 --> 00:08:18,633
PAUL: neither angels nor demons, neither the present nor the future, nor any powers,

134
00:08:18,653 --> 00:08:23,101
PAUL: neither height nor depth, nor anything else in all creation...

135
00:08:23,151 --> 00:08:26,958
PAUL: will be able to separate us from the love of God...

136
00:08:26,978 --> 00:08:30,258
PAUL: that is in Christ Jesus our Lord.

137
00:08:33,008 --> 00:08:37,069
At first light, they led the old man out of the city.

138
00:08:37,419 --> 00:08:43,537
Among the few who walked with him to the end... was the one who had every reason to hate him.

139
00:08:45,487 --> 00:08:48,398
ASHER: Lord... I don't know how to love him yet.

140
00:08:48,847 --> 00:08:50,085
ASHER: Teach me.

141
00:08:52,235 --> 00:08:56,817
JESUS: Learn from me... for I am gentle and humble in heart.

